# Evidence files are byte-exact records, not source, and must survive a
# checkout unchanged.
#
# The generation manifests are written with an explicit verbatim newline by
# platform_core.continuation_task, for a stated reason: "a manifest whose rows
# end differently on two machines is one whose digest differs for a reason
# having nothing to do with the models". manifest_digest hashes those rows, so
# a newline rewritten on checkout changes the digest of a record whose whole
# job is to be comparable across machines.
#
# This repository has core.autocrlf=true and no other .gitattributes, so
# without this rule `git add` warns "LF will be replaced by CRLF the next time
# Git touches it" -- and it would be right. The outcome and comparison records
# get the same treatment for the same reason: they are compared, digested and
# cited, not edited.
#
# -text rather than `text eol=lf`: no conversion in either direction, so the
# bytes committed are the bytes scored.
runs/gen-*/*.jsonl -text
runs/gen-*/*.json -text
